List a card's earlier title and body texts, newest first, as: vN  @editor  time
title. Every edit of the title or body keeps the text it replaced. Bodies are
not listed; with --version N print that past version: a header line, the title
and the body, plus a 'Page:' line when that version had an HTML page. --page
with --version N prints that version's page HTML (exit 3 when none). A full
page ends with the command for older versions.

Examples:
  lorvik history 42
  lorvik history 42 --version 2
  lorvik history 42 --version 2 --page > old.html

Usage
  lorvik history <number> [--version v] [flags]

Flags
      --cursor string   List versions older than this one: the next value printed by a previous page
  -h, --help            help for history
  -L, --limit int       Maximum versions to list (default 10)
      --page            With --version, print that version's HTML page source instead
      --version int     Show this past version

Global flags
      --api-url string   Server URL (default: LORVIK_API_URL)
      --json             Output the raw API JSON
  -p, --project string   Project slug (default: LORVIK_PROJECT or .lorvik.toml)
  -Q, --quiet            Suppress the unread notice on stderr and an empty inbox
      --session string   Session label for this chat (default: LORVIK_SESSION or derived; see lorvik session)
